# Local dev demo overrides. Copy to .env.development.local (NOT .env.local).
#
# Why .env.development.local:
#   Vite reads .env.local for ALL modes including production builds (yarn build).
#   That bakes any internal hostnames or dev-only values into the deployed
#   bundle on staging/prod. Use .env.development.local instead — Vite only
#   loads it for `yarn dev` (development mode), not for `yarn build`. This
#   prevents a .env.local file from leaking through `make ui-quick-deploy`
#   or any production deploy.
#
# Variables you'll typically want for local dev:
VITE_IOT_API_BASE_URL=https://your-local-or-tunneled-iot-api.example.com
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-local-or-tunneled-api.example.com
VITE_COGNITO_DOMAIN=<your-cognito-prefix>.auth.<region>.amazoncognito.com
VITE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/auth/callback

# If your local dev has Federate-style SSO, set the redirect URI to your
# local callback URL — never to an internal company hostname (those would
# get baked into any production build that loads this file by mistake).
#
# `make ui-quick-deploy` runs a pre-sync scan of build/ for internal
# hostnames (<internal-corp-domains>) and refuses
# to deploy if any are found. If the scan trips, the most likely cause
# is a polluted .env.local that crept into the build environment.
